# Git and environments (user decisions 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-24)

Full rules: `docs/agents/git-workflow.md`.

- GitHub holds exactly two branches: `dev` (shared integration source) and `main` (production). Never push or open a PR from any other branch. Never push or merge `main`. Never force-push. Never delete `dev`.
- Flow: verify locally (`scripts/verify.sh`) → land on `dev` (`scripts/land.sh`, fast-forward only) → the user tests locally and approves → the user merges the single release PR `dev → main`.
- Vercel deploys only `main`; preview deployments are disabled. `dev` pushes run CI. Local verification remains required before landing.
- Check `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/dev HEAD` before rebasing. If true, do not rebase. Otherwise use `git -c rebase.updateRefs=false rebase --rebase-merges origin/dev`.
- Local servers: web on port 3000, engine on port 8000, nothing else (`scripts/local-app.sh`). If busy, wait for the owner; never pick another port; stop what you start.
- Children never push or open PRs; the parent lands.
